eld system now but the mapping evidence suggest it was external to it originally with a small paddock, NPRN 529095, to its north. The building measures 14 metres east southeast to west northwest by 4.5 metres.  It comprises two rooms with a broad section of wall at the west northwest end, which may be an extra cell but it is now full of stone.  Beyond that is an extra block of masonry, its purpose unknown. J.J. Hall, Trysor, 19th February 2013', 'resourceinstanceid': '152282d9-e502-43c3-9eab-afd851e0af50', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Groes Fechan, House II ', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '529450', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (dd7aa3f6-2677-4850-b1b2-3e8dab01d48c)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (ea438d8c-a051-40ab-94e2-23dc29a3c654)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (d28cb8c0-2632-44da-9471-b1462b1b0181)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (8957f44a-7ebf-43a4-801a-6a7f5c785f67)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (bca10d1e-3732-41b7-80f8-ee56479a7e92)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (8ce797fd-35a2-4a53-b6a6-574e5f83abbb)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (089de45e-9cd3-4eb7-bcdc-0a2ffe1c8499)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (5c3e79eb-7e9e-49ea-8c8d-d9ab5ca0c6c8)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (22fcb177-f286-4656-b186-109602ca4634)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (e2f439a0-5cdb-4afa-98d8-a95ab40a4282)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (b6c3ccb5-6e09-4ce8-97ce-615e83a8d92b)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (dd45d26a-1775-4ee6-973b-bad0ca1cae80)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (f094a5cc-8568-4e29-843f-1de6134ae416)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (3862eff0-2c21-4db5-bba6-83d9725c84f3)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (88df064f-f801-4c92-b8e1-850e5bcf643b)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (4b3cb9c8-c720-4fa0-826d-e6f6fada1671)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (67626bef-6f21-4e45-a083-7d6bd6e2921b)>], 'strings': [{'string': 'Groes Fechan, House II ', 'nodegroup_