2e8b-f4be-4dab-841d-c4afa0a6f6c6')}], 'points': [{'point': {'lon': -3.9280057, 'lat': 52.175924}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f6a-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}], 'numbers': [{'number': 529456.0, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4f-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}], 'date_ranges': [], 'ids': [], 'provisional_resource': 'false'}}}, {'index': {'_index': 'rcahmw_resources', '_type': '_doc', '_id': '344b4a8c-2a4b-4960-b389-e49ae70a282e', 'status': 404, 'error': {'type': 'index_not_found_exception', 'reason': 'no such index [rcahmw_resources]', 'index_uuid': '4UoPqYUbTbOhxxsTW-tO1Q', 'index': 'rcahmw_resources'}, 'data': {'displaydescription': 'A complex of stony field boundary banks and walls that can only be partly seen now in a sheltered upland valley on the south side of Bryn Poeth, part of a deserted rural settlement, NPRN 529112.  The walls are visible on either side of the valley, but the central part of the valley is obscured by a boggy area into which the boundaries appear to disappear and it is not certain that the enclosures either side of the valley are actually connected to each other, although they seem likely to be contemporary.  The boundary banks to the western side of the valley are typically 1.25 metres wide and up to 1 metre high. They include sections of drystone walling as well as more rounded earth and stone banks, across and area over 250 metres long south-southwest to north-northeast, by 160 metres wide. The boundary banks to the eastern side of the valley are typically of drystone construction, including regular use of edge-set slabs.  The field system extends, across and area over 225 metres long south-southwest to north-northeast, by about 100 metres wide.  Cultivation marks can be seen within part of if it. Much of the area is now bracken covered, which hinders recording and interpretation. An estate map of 1791 drawn by Thomas Lewis of Lands in the Parish of Prysg and Carfan shows the outer boundary of the field system.  None of the buildings are shown which suggests that they were no longer used at this time but the field system was still recognised. R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 27 March 2013', 'resourceinstanceid': '344b4a8c-2a4b-4960-b389-e49ae70a282e', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Cae Penygraig, Bryn Poeth, Field System', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '529457', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (15388eb7-eb2c-4941-ac33-33ee080573f1)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (7b58e3f3-4597-4b23-b00e-877d6c151814)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (866a351b-ad43-4969-b2e8-8c1b60bf6b34)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (102ed609-27a3-466c-8eb4-6d5cef7641ba)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (fa752b53-9e40-452a-b4d1-8cec072851f2)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (ba930a34-2049-4866-bd26-ae49ec3a343a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (23672585-2246-47db-ab87-67f8b129b168)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (e987a57f-d312-44db-976c-4c508012b097)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (38eeb97f-fc52-45a9-be4d-7da438b6f894)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (c5a3666d-4150-46c2-9e6f-4878cf7a9630)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (43a2bf60-f60c-46e9-bdbb-2aafb37a31ee)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (505a9445-3e4c-49b7-a9d9-9d86d86baa77)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (4326544d-e1f2-473f-9977-d3bcf3692d8a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (5d5390ac-afc5-4a9f-b9b6-8a4843348c67)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (631cb37e-2ecc-4bd4-85fc-ae8e30f1c738)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (77a19f1e-b4ca-473c-ae9e-d6a706eba93c)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (06ec78a8-c720-4f47-a074-c0fc21a10587)>], 'strings': [{'string': 'Cae Penygraig, Bryn Poeth, Field System', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'No preference', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'A complex of stony field boundary banks and walls that can only be partly seen now in a sheltered upland valley on the south side of Bryn Poeth, part of a deserted rural settlement, NPRN 529112.  The walls are visible on either side of the valley, but the central part of the valley is obscured by a boggy area into which the boundaries appear to disappear and it is not certain that the enclosures either side of the valley are actually connected to each other, although they seem likely to be contemporary.  The boundary banks to the western side of the valley are typically 1.25 metres wide and up to 1 metre high. They include sections of drystone walling as well as more rounded earth and stone banks, across and area over 250 metres long south-southwest to north-northeast, by 160 metres wide. The boundary banks to the eastern side of the valley are typically of drystone construction, including regular use of edge-set slabs.  The field system extends, across and area over 225 metres long south-southwest to north-northeast, by about 100 metres wide.  Cultivation marks can be seen within part of if it. Much of the area is now bracken covered, which hinders recording and interpretation. An estate map of 1791 drawn by Thomas Lewis of Lands in the Parish of Prysg and Carfan shows the outer boundary of the field system.  None of the buildings are shown which suggests that they were no longer used at this time but the field system was still recognised. R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 27 March 2013', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'English Description', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'SN6825054905', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f67-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704')}, {'string': 'SN6854', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'SN65SE', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Grid refe