04'), 'provisional': False}], 'date_ranges': [], 'ids': [], 'provisional_resource': 'false'}}}, {'index': {'_index': 'rcahmw_resources', '_type': '_doc', '_id': '42a9b10e-0f79-4497-8646-224c872839d8', 'status': 404, 'error': {'type': 'index_not_found_exception', 'reason': 'no such index [rcahmw_resources]', 'index_uuid': '4UoPqYUbTbOhxxsTW-tO1Q', 'index': 'rcahmw_resources'}, 'data': {'displaydescription': 'A large, drystone sheep fold, located in a sheltered valley to the south of Bryn Poeth. It lies within a field system (NPRN 529457) but is clearly later as stone has evidently been robbed from the field boundary walls to construct the fold.  The fold itself measures about 14 metres east to west, by 9 metres wide.  Its strongly built walls stand up to 1 metre high and are 0.70 metres wide.  At its southern side it incorporates a natural stone outcrop into its structure. The entrance is in the western end of the northern wall, which leads into a narrow, western compartment. Another entrance leads through the eastern side of this compartment into the main part of the fold.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 27 March 2013', 'resourceinstanceid': '42a9b10e-0f79-4497-8646-224c872839d8', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Bryn Poeth, Fold', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '529494', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (8e4f5b11-2495-4e5c-8106-af7e33851ddc)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (116b193d-fac9-4c39-95fc-a1147c5fdee9)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (6e673cb7-3c89-4441-81a9-404935a3e5bb)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (b073768a-8690-4100-a939-86f9f61e6973)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (bd24ff3e-7cd7-4946-9f14-4da5ffa692f7)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (35fc2b10-f94f-4509-ab3d-bf3611dd7609)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (b55bc35e-1fad-4506-80f2-45dad59724b4)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (00b3fbed-6ffd-4ed6-b8c1-38caec1cfd7a)>, <TileModel: TileMod