', 'index': 'rcahmw_resources'}, 'data': {'displaydescription': 'This drystone structure is one in a group of long huts and other settlement features in a sheltered valley to the south side of Bryn Poeth.  This feature, now covered in grass and bracken, may be a fold. It is rectilinear and measures 5.5 metres long, south-southeast to north-northwest, by 5 metres wide.  Its low walls are up to 1 metre wide and built of stone blocks.  At the southern end, internally, there are several edge set slabs against the side of the wall.  An enclosure bank runs to meet the northwestern corner of the structure.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 28 March 2013', 'resourceinstanceid': '4fdb361c-8b95-48cd-9d67-bcc3f11b8b42', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Cae Penygraig, Bryn Poeth, Structure II ', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '529496', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (94fb2fed-9386-4228-8355-a9c28d42217c)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (52e2f7a6-b09f-4f48-abba-6fea1d987bc4)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a0c4be42-baf8-4796-9904-0a79280ff030)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (ee5887dc-d8a8-4c0d-b0d2-a98e7bc2fa27)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (7869df0c-4cb1-4c97-a0f3-bf274edb282d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a2389a2c-c9d6-49d4-9f97-4f88b79c0e2a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (853c026b-ad33-4a67-9bc9-a6cc2fe1624d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (52207133-2768-4598-9e06-61b0673c7327)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (6fc0e4b5-8423-452b-95d8-2e22245dbb9c)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (e7804178-d890-4559-991b-3869c332544c)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (3a36e4f0-4e36-4343-8de3-44883abd0a59)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (04526b61-8a82-4e7c-ad50-dc347bb51de6)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (f291625b-7b22-4fc2-8a60-65f03fbc797c)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (fa279d16-394b-4c23-b988-394e611f06c9)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (c5860dc1-409b-46bd-949f-7aeb