tructure is difficult to interpret as it is obscured by thick reed growth that hides many details of its character.   Two parallel stone banks can be discerned, which are perhaps as much as 14 metres long, east-northeast by west-southwest, and 3 metres wide overall.  This gives the structure the appearance of a large sunken shelter.  At the western end the southern wall seems to turn to the west-northwest, creating an entrance 0.80 metres wide into the space between the two banks, which is reminiscent of the type of offset entrances displayed by many sunken shelters in Ceredigion.  The southern wall is a revetment wall, built against the natural slope, whilst the northern wall is free-standing and up to 1 metre wide and 0.30 metres thick.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 28 March 2013', 'resourceinstanceid': '76a0cb81-794f-4878-81ff-fe928ecc0e7b', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Waun Clawdd, Structure II ', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '529501', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (24ce96c9-80b2-4691-b984-ad8ea3cfac9e)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (244b2f45-d3e8-4f16-ad8d-66cd503d87d9)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (4bd1fc89-fc0b-4c7c-827c-1b09ea9cfc6a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (dde67385-eaf9-4371-a284-8de230fd57c6)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (455ff095-b259-49e6-b081-fa11a6420539)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (e87a0e83-a11c-4eec-be42-2d483dc0c3e4)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (23871c9b-76c3-4245-b18b-631409bc32bc)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (61b96f56-b0cd-445b-bea4-d2e886b30b1d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (10d5da3b-58cb-4b2c-b89a-b37b242e772d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (907101ce-1a3a-473b-ae31-30a12ee3a338)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (35bcafcb-e636-4623-9e47-6b5dc8161497)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (366f5ba8-46f2-4bdf-9687-78487e231ad9)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (34c9d96b-3330-49bc-87e3-13a6ef22592b)>, 