_resources]', 'index_uuid': '4UoPqYUbTbOhxxsTW-tO1Q', 'index': 'rcahmw_resources'}, 'data': {'displaydescription': 'An earthwork platform situated close to the boundary between the mountain pasture and enclosed farmland on the steep, northwest facing slope of Banc y Gwyngoed. It is the largest in a pair of platforms, the other one being NPRN 529505.   It measures at least 10.5 metres long, north-northwest to south-southeast.  It is cut relatively deeply into the slope, with its fan rising 1.5 metres high to its southern side, whilst its apron at the southern end is also quite pronounced and some 2 metres high.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 28 March 2013', 'resourceinstanceid': '5de700e1-db0a-416a-b218-779c56afcb6c', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Banc y Gwyngoed, Platform II ', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '529506', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (3f98df87-bccf-476e-a480-7a6abb89ec5e)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (39086010-ee74-4aa2-bc4d-c6e2afa9345c)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (1995ab67-a614-47a1-98ca-005aac1b77c1)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (55e97a22-aa70-4f90-bad4-9d2d059be3bc)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (386a39bd-0801-465d-92e3-f7966582284f)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (d775858b-df56-4bb4-ab69-b615aa511fc3)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (87d3f630-8ffc-408c-b203-27e8dca2524f)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (be59a2d2-1a88-45e4-b62a-0e6ebb96538b)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (c92b3922-b5a4-4b6c-96a0-127a82639fff)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (01f1079c-e90d-4677-aa62-bda52b72bbc5)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (3170b03e-296b-422f-8bbd-530406053544)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (b3f4e7be-183c-48ac-98f6-1ecb7a503c08)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (7599af5e-ca8e-4a30-a08e-8edef5953335)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (24802729-1d60-41a6-a13d-e942af7e7d41)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (28dec527-de77-4681-bf92-fb48