 UUID('60120f46-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'CHAMBERED CAIRN', 'conceptid': UUID('a7160cc9-7586-3c17-b80d-46034a5fc542'), 'valueid': '03aa1912-7c3c-438b-9a6b-b834abd2b9ca', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'No Preference', 'conceptid': UUID('bdf4c70c-6a13-4cd0-a33f-33241d81302e'), 'valueid': '078fdac7-cb0c-4ab6-b252-0db193d97a9c', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'Possible Type', 'conceptid': UUID('87a03b9b-5305-4ba1-8f7d-a6c705c2369a'), 'valueid': '5dba2e8c-26c3-4ae9-9223-69dd2f3917b4', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': '1D', 'conceptid': UUID('6cc63e17-2fb0-4833-b6dd-892ae684cbb9'), 'valueid': 'f70555f5-5981-4f8d-bea0-ded6fa05120e', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f55-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'Not Applicable', 'conceptid': UUID('d131c30a-ae2b-45a1-a9b8-c118e0ef1e32'), 'valueid': '54496ff2-4693-4138-ba03-277eff940f11', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f55-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'PRN', 'conceptid': UUID('06018787-add2-4b63-970b-c58102be0ecc'), 'valueid': 'd7df4ea2-407f-44a1-93fa-171a86536818', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f52-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'Dyfed Historic Environment Record', 'conceptid': UUID('444b6617-4fea-41a2-be4d-5e30768efaa5'), 'valueid': '7392fc95-d2ba-4ac9-a33c-9028d817790c', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f52-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'Not Applicable', 'conceptid': UUID('d131c30a-ae2b-45a1-a9b8-c118e0ef1e32'), 'valueid': '54496ff2-4693-4138-ba03-277eff940f11', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f5b-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'Earthwork', 'conceptid': UUID('f2d530fa-5e40-4237-8885-bf635f02dd88'), 'valueid': '54d7e6d4-4604-49ee-a027-021778082062', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f5b-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'Neolithic', 'conceptid': UUID('ef9cf57d-b902-4c5e-a60f-56a995bf21dc'), 'valueid': '8d8fe8e1-0d15-40e5-b4fc-74da7812d4a7', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f58-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'Possible Type', 'conceptid': UUID('87a03b9b-5305-4ba1-8f7d-a6c705c2369a'), 'valueid': '5dba2e8c-26c3-4ae9-9223-69dd2f3917b4', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f58-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'label': 'No Preference', 'conceptid': UUID('bdf4c70c-6a13-4cd0-a33f-33241d81302e'), 'valueid': '078fdac7-cb0c-4ab6-b252-0db193d97a9c', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f58-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}], 'geometries': [{'geom': {'type': 'FeatureCollection', 'features': [{'id': 'eb4ad6b5-903f-440e-b465-ff64b61d6c2c', 'type': 'Feature', 'geometry': {'type': 'Point', 'coordinates': [-3.92613, 52.189038]}, 'properties': {}}]}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f6a-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False, 'tileid': UUID('02731ce5-1128-44dc-a968-394a6e3e3f5e')}], 'points': [{'point': {'lon': -3.92613, 'lat': 52.189038}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f6a-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}], 'numbers': [{'number': 529508.0, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4f-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}], 'date_ranges': [], 'ids': [], 'provisional_resource': 'false'}}}, {'index': {'_index': 'rcahmw_resources', '_type': '_doc', '_id': '8cae6b61-5f14-40f4-899f-009d87c41788', 'status': 404, 'error': {'type': 'index_not_found_exception', 'reason': 'no such index [rcahmw_resources]', 'index_uuid': '4UoPqYUbTbOhxxsTW-tO1Q', 'index': 'rcahmw_resources'}, 'data': {'displaydescription': "This unusual monument appears to be an example of a Neolithic chambered cairn, which is a rare site type in southwest and midwest Wales.  Cerrig Clochesti was first described by Ceredigion antiquarian Trevor Lewis in 1927, when he part excavated the site, although did not appreciate its unique characteristic in terms of Ceredigion's prehistoric monuments.  Today it survives as a complex of features, most important of which are two large slabs of stone which were the capstones that originally covered two separate underground cists.  Before Lewis recorded the site in 1927, these capstones had already been dragged off their chambers. <br>\n<br>\nThis record relates to the western cist.  This seems to have been the smallest of the pair and, unlike its eastern neighbour, is not obviously associated with a stone cairn, although the thick grass and bilberry over the site may obscure such features.  The site was noted by Paul Sambrook during the 1990s and recorded in the regional Sites and Monuments Record at that time.  It was noted then that both cists were lined with drystone revetment walls, although by 2012 denser vegetation across the site effectively obscures this detail.  The cist is now about 1.75 metres long by 1.5 metres wide and 0.7 metres deep.  Lewis, in 1927, recorded that the cists here were up to `four feet? deep.  The capstone that once covered the cist is a very large slab of stone.  It measures about 2 metres square and is at least 0.25 metres thick.  The slab has been dragged a short distance downslope to the north, and now lies immediately below the cist.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 28 March 2013", 'resourceinstanceid': '8cae6b61-5f14-40f4-899f-009d87c41788', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Cerrig Clochesti, Cist', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '529509', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (a356de0a-bdc7-4bd4-967c-d3a0279bffab)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (3cbc12b3-5c43-49f8-a5f2-5f00ad49486d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (be2a7ad9-0707-45a3-8bd0-e05ad5f800cc)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (c94978ab-4109-4d4b-98d0-105f8b415dd7)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (3574916d-739e-4fb0-be9b-5ea870b7108d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (f5fc6a80-2ed1-4a0d-8f75-0d62c0c549ea)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (d33c67bd-aabc-4c40-81d2-d0143ab095f7)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (faf8d7dc-819a-43bd-b986-23289ca817d2)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (cd21e0b6-e867-455b-ab36-37dbeaabd40b)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (12635dd5-f0da-414f-baaa-412e9acaa02a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a20f82bf-3b00-4b52-82dd-9e9e5cde19f8)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (14e209dc-c4c5-4d6c-80f0-67de137b33f9)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (f0050718-7c48-4846-93ff-1be13ecd92c7)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (ddff9cbb-bfb9-459b-abe6-d9f0060aaa44)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (249084ff-dbe4-4341-b53e-7cc915177929)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (41aa43e8-3e32-42f2-9329-a72b17486903)>], 'strings': [{'string': 'Cerrig Clochesti, Cist', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'No preference', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': "This unusual monument appears to be an example of a Neolithic chambered cairn, which is a rare site type in southwest and midwest Wales.  Cerrig Clochesti was first described by Ceredigion antiquarian Trevor Lewis in 1927, when he part excavated the site, although did not appreciate its unique characteristic in terms of Ceredigion's prehistoric monuments.  Today it survives as a complex of features, most important of which are two large slabs of stone which were the capstones that originally covered two separate underground cists.  Before Lewis recorded the site in 1927, these capstones had already been dragged off their chambers. <br>\n<br>\nThis record relates to the western cist.  This seems to have been the smallest of the pair and, unlike its eastern neighbour, is not obviously associated with a stone cairn, although the thick grass and bilberry over the site may obscure such features.  The site was noted by Paul Sambrook during the 1990s and recorded in the regional Sites and Monuments Record at that time.  It was noted then that both cists were lined with drystone revetment walls, although by 2012 denser vegetation across the site effectively obscures this detail.  The cist is now about 1.75 metres long by 1.5 metres wide and 0.7 metres deep.  Lewis, in 1927, recorded that the cists here were up to `four feet? deep.  The capstone that once covered the cist is a very large slab of stone.  It measures about 2 metres square and is at least 0.25 metres thick.  The slab has been dragged a short distance downslope to the north, and now lies immediately below the cist.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 28 March 2013", 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'English Description', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'SN6842356285', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f67-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704')}, {'string': 'SN6856', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'SN65NE', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Grid reference taken at centre of site', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'JJH', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('0b5446f8-a00c-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Llanddewi Brefi', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f3d-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Cardiganshire', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f61-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Ceredigion', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f46-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'CIST', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'No Preference', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string':