s a fold (NPRN 529026), a long hut (NPRN 529029) and three potato clamps (NPRNs 529030-529032), set within earth-banked enclosures with evidence of lazy bed cultivation (NPRN 529028).  The potato clamps indicate that this is a post medieval settlement, but it does not appear on 19th century Ordnance Survey maps, including the 1819 Original Surveyors drawings, which suggests a pre-19th century date.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 26 March 2013', 'resourceinstanceid': '2adb27fd-660f-4865-8024-0f4cf2ba6e41', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Esgair Hir, Settlement', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '529595', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (e1281eb8-4027-4281-a5e1-eb710947df83)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (823dc632-8c17-4a78-8dd2-fb3d7ee76aee)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (4ea9a87b-f45f-4e57-a53d-2a4072ac57a6)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (77ba726b-9bc2-4a4a-a852-1e0e105d067e)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (89666bd9-8976-4c2b-959c-9eaab256bf1c)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (8c883ae4-c6ed-437f-8c39-09e799c079f6)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (69354918-e7a8-41bd-a89c-b5f857a72c20)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (913ba68b-5515-4f74-8c59-f29a5bf43895)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (0fe27676-da28-4d96-b878-a9effac7231b)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (39b914c4-a9ae-45b1-b43f-c2b374732ba6)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a746535f-efdc-40d8-b78e-e2f69b37864b)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (bd9315b3-1c27-4dfe-81e4-acd6d5be9c2b)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (dc71735f-ce75-4d69-85e6-ad50fd65cfbf)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (76ce0489-2c79-4f6e-ab04-a9d74089972a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (54d96301-121c-450f-977f-9cc44f40234a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (d246f071-bc2d-4fad-9c92-6ed7a4e588c5)>], 'strings': [{'string': 'Esgair Hir, Settlement', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'stri