r to be marker stones contemporary with the cairn.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 26 March 2013', 'resourceinstanceid': '652c1da0-9c2d-48a2-8047-562b9212753b', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Bryn Rhudd, Ring Cairn III', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '529607', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (dd5f5b4e-fe6a-4911-8db0-775d82c4c5ec)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a0c78573-7911-47a4-a9e5-72a5134a1b3e)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (6936473b-1dfa-441a-ae2b-becf207aca64)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (bdf32c54-e56b-4567-8e2a-a8a7244b883f)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (71ce4726-3695-468b-a99c-93fed86dec7a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (cc7ca9bf-b996-4151-a3fb-0bfb57dd97c2)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (ba0c931a-e735-46c3-b975-c4199bd78647)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (e2ed0f31-e39e-4e20-9151-d6dfd4d1d8ed)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (854f6ba6-9538-4ba4-9b22-2ef5f5f89657)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (5926dca7-e56a-4e1a-9b28-a3119843cc5e)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (52813a54-4d3a-4c0c-9724-c3f86801794d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (10471ac3-b09d-46c6-ad85-ef5fb1281ee2)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (b3a1dd69-669f-42be-b009-9d8f8d5151ec)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (13a07501-20e3-4670-9399-68d2ece4d0fd)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a5ac8d6f-6dcc-4ba8-8c28-c3cd5cd78a8c)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (7986fd9e-8cdf-4a01-8ee2-305848eff24d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (7aa03f28-1a3b-4bcf-a37b-b027258247c6)>], 'strings': [{'string': 'Bryn Rhudd, Ring Cairn III', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'No preference', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'A well-preserved Bronze Age ring cairn, slightly oval in plan, which measures 10.5 metres east to west, by 12.5 metres.   The stony ring which defines the monument is up to 2.5 metres wide and 0.25 metres high. The hollow at the centre of the cairn is sunk down perhaps 0.30 metres lower than the surrounding landscape and has stone scattered within it.  There is a possible cist cover exposed within the hollow.  Two monoliths stand close to this cairn, NPRN 529033 being 24 metres to the southwest and NPRN 529034 standing about 35 metres to the west. These appear to be marker stones contemporary with the cairn.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 26 March 2013', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'English Description', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'SN6899555097', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f67-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704')}, {'string': 'SN6855', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'SN65NE', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Grid reference taken at centre of site', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'RPS', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('0b5446f8-a00c-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Llanddewi Brefi', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f3d-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Cardiganshire', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f61-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Ceredigion', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f46-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'RING CAIRN', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'No Preference', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Not Applicable', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': '2B', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f55-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'