is Bronze Age cairn cemetery was discovered in 1998 during a Cadw-funded Deserted Rural Settlements survey by the Dyfed Archaeological Trust.  It was subsequently revisited by the Trust as part of the Cadw-funded Prehistoric Funerary and Ritual Monuments Survey.  Originally, as many as seven small cairns were noted, including one with an open cist (NPRN 403851, now scheduled as Cm363), which indicated that this was indeed a group of funerary cairns.  The cairns were mostly low, circular stone mounds, measuring between 3 metres and 4 metres in diameter. Apart from NPRN 403851 they appeared to be undisturbed.<br>\n  <br>\nThe cairns were revisited by Trysor as part of the South West Cambrians Uplands Initiative survey in early March 2013. Ground conditions were favourable, thanks to a prolonged cold, dry spell. Ground vegetation, chiefly grasses, was at a minimum.  Even so, it was found that there had been a considerable increase in ground vegetation cover since 1998.  As a result only 4 of the 7 cairns reported in 1998 were traceable.  These are NPRN 403851, NPRNs 529534 and 529691, which are both at the eastern edge of a modern trackway that runs to a gate through a boundary fence, some 35 metres to their north-northeast, and NPRN 529693, at the southern edge of the cairn cemetery area.  It is presumed that the remaining three cairns described in the regional HER are all now obscured beneath the grass cover.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 28 March 2013', 'resourceinstanceid': '15f01119-c332-4623-8b13-e8a25a06d9b3', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Craig Twrch, Cairn Cemetery', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '529692', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (db361eb0-56f6-4d51-bdf2-3ac10d598ba6)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a4098b62-0834-40bc-8beb-94a79d40fe29)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (b04ee75e-7ed4-4b34-914f-97a34c8a164d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (2f2ee9f3-5023-4b94-91f8-3395ccf816bf)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (4412dd84-09cf-4651-9ce0-73eaa6e83a91)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (4a74893f-d108-4d24-90c9-be8029fec9a6)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a62f9191-23c3-422e-b153-147c605e7540)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (efa4e7ad-021f-4fb9-96f6-36367c1123b0)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (5a55f366-833d-4169-a741-372ff1b42a07)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (662fc523-237a-4e1e-a444-401ad7bac1ac)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (af504c1f-d377-4758-83fb-a33555baae60)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (c41c56fa-fe0e-48b2-84f2-d1f89c18fca2)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (030b49a0-6435-4e92-9cb0-f84981cc1f5d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (6a9a3b31-a89e-42b1-bc2a-3640da74b8b8)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (0089717e-e999-43aa-95c3-0efd3652bdc9)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (bb8d4d5d-a14b-4a78-a85c-e09310f6f2fb)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (fe3352d4-9603-4043-aef2-789ee90ec090)>], 'strings': [{'string': 'Craig Twrch, Cairn Cemetery', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'No preference', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'This Bronze Age cairn cemetery was discovered in 1998 during a Cadw-funded Deserted Rural Settlements survey by the Dyfed Archaeological Trust.  It was subsequently revisited by the Trust as part of the Cadw-funded Prehistoric Funerary and Ritual Monuments Survey.  Originally, as many as seven small cairns were noted, including one with an open cist (NPRN 403851, now scheduled as Cm363), which indicated that this was indeed a group of funerary cairns.  The cairns were mostly low, circular stone mounds, measuring between 3 metres and 4 metres in diameter. Apart from NPRN 403851 they appeared to be undisturbed.<br>\n  <br>\nThe cairns were revisited by Trysor as part of the South West Cambrians Uplands Initiative survey in early March 2013. Ground conditions were favourable, thanks to a prolonged cold, dry spell. Ground vegetation, chiefly grasses, was at a minimum.  Even so, it was found that there had been a considerable increase in ground vegetation cover since 1998.  As a result only 4 of the 7 cairns reported in 1998 were traceable.  These are NPRN 403851, NPRNs 529534 and 529691, which are both at the eastern edge of a modern trackway that runs to a gate through a boundary fence, some 35 metres to their north-northeast, and NPRN 529693, at the southern edge of the cairn cemetery area.  It is presumed that the remaining three cairns described in the regional HER are all now obscured beneath the grass cover.  R.P. Sambrook, Trysor, 28 March 2013', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'English Description', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'SN6617549112', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f67-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704')}, {'string': 'SN6649', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'SN64NE', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Grid reference taken at centre of site', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'JJH', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('0b5446f8-a00c-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Cynwyl Gaeo', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f3d-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Carmarthenshire', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f61-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'Carmarthenshire', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f46-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'CAIRN CEMETERY', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'provisional': False}, {'string': 'No Preference', 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'prov