_found_exception', 'reason': 'no such index [rcahmw_resources]', 'index_uuid': '4UoPqYUbTbOhxxsTW-tO1Q', 'index': 'rcahmw_resources'}, 'data': {'displaydescription': 'A roughly triangular enclosure, within an area measuring 50m by 30m, with a rectangular sheepfold (feature 530058) attached to its southwest end. The drystone walls of the enclosure survive up to 1.5m in height and 0.75m in width. The southeast wall of the enclosure is approximately 40m in length. A filled in sheep-crawl can be seen near its south end. The northeast wall is approximately 32m in length, with an entrance to the enclosure situated approximately 12m from its western corner. The northwest wall is approximately 44m in length. A drystone wall extends to the northeast from the eastern corner of the enclosure, approximately 13m long, and a second drystone wall 30m in length extends to the north 5m northwest of the entrance to the enclosure, following the contour of the hill slope. The feature is depicted on the 1901 25 inch OS map. T. Burke-Davies, ArcHeritage, 18 May 2012.', 'resourceinstanceid': 'c667302e-f0cf-4372-af4c-024b48a253f9', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Ffridd Dalcen, Enclosure I', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '530059', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (a69604c5-5b82-4f10-bf49-fec1a25eabba)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (af97bb83-768f-435a-b715-25e96e23e225)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a5c54c11-2728-4e6e-af60-37ea9cd56497)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (31267512-d65f-4ce5-868c-ede4014a6719)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (58de088f-9fca-4592-b56c-08106db9a452)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (990c18db-622c-46b2-9753-8f8ee89d9430)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (3729f7e5-234b-4678-a380-8ac0158b018c)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (40caa36f-2f23-47a3-96bd-e24f7d2a1910)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (c74b1259-6f5d-489d-a5e1-e1e85b0ffed4)>, <Tile