dth. The walls are 0.5m in width. The building appears to have been cut into the natural hill side, and the maximum internal height is 2m, with an external height of 0.5m. The structure is aligned east to west, with the east end having the best preservation and the west end suffering substantial damage, resulting in a large stone spread from wall collapse. No internal divisions are visible within the structure. There appears to be an adjoining structure of earlier construction comprising earth and stone banks attached to the north side of the main structure. This may have been an enclosure, covering an area of 10 square metres. The banks are 1m in width and ranging from 0.5m to 1.0m in height.There are two boundary banks (features 530137 and 530138) in close proximity. It is depicted on the 1889, 1901 and 1953 OS maps. A. Farrington-McCabe, ArcHeritage, 16 May 2012.', 'resourceinstanceid': '9d0ed1ab-0e4d-4aeb-8c02-d9cb37e8b0f1', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Dol-y-Moch-Isaf, Farmstead I', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '530137', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (ecffa572-ca47-40bc-a4c7-5d788c8a74c0)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (5b53ef26-4e63-4701-97bc-4ad75fd86ea7)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (3b55d15d-cbbc-46cb-b28d-7dd0c939e18a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (c6fa09af-70a2-43c0-8f31-86cb4fc0d1f0)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (bdb93657-cef5-4172-8dee-42c5a9497081)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (cbc9619f-7cea-4155-a014-854a1cdc989f)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (12845432-1ada-410f-8191-9db3a7856fb0)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (89bdb90e-7c66-4b09-b6f8-7bcff8877f4f)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (ce7a8ba5-6b62-4b54-86be-41c744a61411)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (b365256e-9c35-4dd9-ac02-59ac05730122)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (f5ad9e8a-90b7-4d68-9764-037a68211269)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (6ff91a1d-f325-4b