e': '_doc', '_id': '1d8073e7-6ae2-42d8-ac42-a364344b50bb', 'status': 404, 'error': {'type': 'index_not_found_exception', 'reason': 'no such index [rcahmw_resources]', 'index_uuid': '4UoPqYUbTbOhxxsTW-tO1Q', 'index': 'rcahmw_resources'}, 'data': {'displaydescription': 'A sub-rectangular field enclosed by low drystone walls, located at the east end of a longer boundary wall (feature 530176). The ground cover is mostly grass, and there are many small mortar craters within the field. The walls of the enclosure are between 0.4 and 0.7m in height, and 0.5-0.7m wide. The wall at the west side has been broken towards the north end for a modern farm track, and there is a possible original gateway at the southern end. There are some areas of wall collapse on the other walls. The south wall of the enclosure is built against the side of a hollow way (530185) and clearly post-dates it. There is a possible gateway at the south end of the eastern wall. The wall along the north side is a continuation of the more extensive field wall 530176. It has a low sheep-crawl built into it. The field is depicted on the 1953 6 inch OS map. R. May, ArcHeritage, 17 May 2012.', 'resourceinstanceid': '1d8073e7-6ae2-42d8-ac42-a364344b50bb', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Ffridd Dol-y-Moch, Field I', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '530192', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (818e6317-33e3-4d7f-9536-78bfced9222d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (878acc5e-962f-42c0-996e-1bbaa5b9b7fe)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (e8781178-5eb0-4207-8e00-1d57aab7f93f)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (c4d7bfd8-ec12-41ba-bec1-e6ad71f56950)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a9640699-0a47-4657-9d75-0880f5f810a1)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (96cd01c7-762d-4f6d-919d-b15cb22246cd)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (8afd6aa3-8ee5-48aa-b320-4b13068c6d04)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (74f7c0d8-f301