ce. The rubble therefore could be the remains of building debris. There is no faced stone visible within the bank, though the building could have been of drystone or rubble construction. The bank is aligned southwest-northeast. It is not precisely on the site of the Dol-y-Mynach-Uchaf farmstead depicted on the 1889 and 1901 25 inch OS maps, which was located c.70m to the northeast, but it could represent a stack of rubble from the demolished house. A. Farrington-McCabe, ArcHeritage, 23 May 2012.', 'resourceinstanceid': '68c8b4ba-2ba3-4781-b787-b355c4a29e69', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'East of Pont Dol-y-Mynach, Bank II ', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '530252', 'tiles': [<TileModel: TileModel object (f8a1c07f-7d39-4b83-ace6-6d8bc605f502)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (ab588be9-c2e2-4b5c-b209-f25d09e50697)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (a1b74a4d-c6dc-487e-a1ec-d5806dab25ba)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (5b190226-ad7e-40f7-b754-ddfda161c997)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (dbfacf46-6fca-4ad3-a464-ecc7a318a74a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (3171ab8d-59de-41cf-bb69-81395e98b698)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (ec0f1930-128e-49d4-a1c8-291e35476f48)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (7a20e6ec-522f-4252-9e4c-487fd3cbab4d)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (b7677306-67f6-4666-9e98-15d3f1c30ebf)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (86b2eb06-4fff-4d88-aba0-3570f4b19608)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (1978065d-d9ad-485f-a8ee-91006894505a)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (68cbfea8-8a22-47fd-aa19-2def383b3d66)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (feb8c0c7-51a9-448a-b4b4-e13b9aafd27b)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (e0640693-2db7-4fc5-858f-419d98eeeef3)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (45e6635a-595d-409e-a907-c32c1ff90081)>, <TileModel: TileModel object (9389df84-e862-4557-a192-49e7e6a1cd75)>], 'strings': [{'string': 'East of Pont Dol-y-Mynach, Bank II ', 'nod