2022-03-01 14:53:15,511 arches.app.search.search WARNING  2022-03-01 14:53:15.509754: WARNING: failed to index document: {'displaydescription': 'Although Glanusk House has been demolished, its park, overlooked by  Penmyarth, occupies an important and picturesque location in the upper Usk valley and survives in its entirety. There are still  remnants of an extensive parterre garden, water garden, pleasure grounds and a walled kitchen garden with a  grotto. The surrounding parkland is also designed.<br>\n<br>\nThe remains of a High Victorian garden by Markham Nesfield laid out between 1842-74 lie next to the house site. A fine new rose garden was planted and belongs to the period after 1986. The Ordnance Survey 25 inch plans are of particular interest in showing changes to the detail of the kitchen garden. There were extensive glasshouses which have now gone, all organised outside the walls, together with a sundial and fountain. They also depict the terraces that stretched out towards the River to then north of the House. Balustrading and steps also survive from Nesfield design.<br>\n<br>\nC.S.Briggs, RCAHMW 5 January 2006<br>\n', 'resourceinstanceid': 'ce15e4ee-e8bb-4bfe-ac02-32e4715a5668', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Glanusk Garden, Llangattock', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '86056', 'tiles': [{'tileid': '7477d214-fd89-4410-80f2-3b740e097aed', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('ce15e4ee-e8bb-4bfe-ac02-32e4715a5668'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f64-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': '9d8460a4-130e-43d2-a50e-ce6dcbbff32f', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('ce15e4ee-e8bb-4bfe-ac02-32e4715a5668'), 'parenttile_id': UUID('7477d214-fd89-4410-80f2-3b740e097aed'), 'data': {'60120f3d-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': 'a8ce5d3c-c1c1-4857-8a8c-432c00f20840'}, 'nodegroup_id': UUI