2022-05-19 11:53:10,170 arches.app.search.search WARNING  2022-05-19 11:53:10.168589: WARNING: failed to index document: {'displaydescription': "Margam Park is a multi-layered site of outstanding historical importance. It includes prehistoric and Cistercian abbey remains, and has a Tudor deer park, eighteenth-century and nineteenth-century garden and landscaping phases. The site is usefully depicted on an early bird's eye view. Of particular importance are the very fine walled deer park, the banqueting house facade, the outstanding Georgian orangery, the Citrus House and the nineteenth-century gardens with their fine collection of trees and shrubs. The 1950s garden of Twyn-yr-hydd is a delightful and well preserved period piece within the park.  Its main dates are from twelfth-fifteenth century; 1540-late seventeenth century; 1786-90; 1830-40; 1920s; 1950s. There are a number of earthworks of possible garden origin.<br>\n<br>\nThe garden is depicted on the Second Edition Ordnance Survey 25-inch map of Glamorgan XXXIII, sheet  7 (1899). Its main elements on that map include greenhouse, terrace walls, antiquity (contrived), saw mill, nursery, woodland with vista paths, woodland, walled garden, well, sundial, relict hedgelines, isolated geometric copses, orangery, carriage drive, waterfall, lodge, parterres, orchard, parkland, pinery, ponds, pheasantry and fountain.<br>\n<br>\nC.H. Nicholas, RCAHMW, 18 August 2006.", 'resourceinstanceid': '02d10841-1c55-43e1-bcfd-a217a0e9df34', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Margam Park Garden, Margam', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '265727', 'tiles': [{'tileid': '64177c0e-16a1-442c-b5fb-b82d501269bd', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('02d10841-1c55-43e1-bcfd-a217a0e9df34'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f64-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {