2022-06-06 15:54:01,659 arches.app.search.search WARNING  2022-06-06 15:54:01.656533: WARNING: failed to index document: {'displaydescription': 'Parklands & Gardens of Wales No:PGW.PO33    <br>\nPark/gardens/landscape features associated with Gregynog Hall (Nprn29283).<br>\nAssociated with: Earthwork features WNW of Hall (Nprn400946).<br>\nRCAHMW AP94-CS 0071<br>\n<br>\n1. GREGYNOG Is one of the most important gardens and parks Formal and informal woodland garden,  in Powys incorporating various historic overlays dating from at least 1500.  William Emes produced proposals in 1774 and some of them were carried out. In 1920 it became the home of the artistic patrons Gwendoline and Margaret Davies.  H. A. Tipping worked on the gardens 1930-33 and Dame Sylvia Crowe in 1972. Dates and creators are c. 1500 on.  House rebuilt c. 1830 and c. 1880. with landscaping/garden making: William Emes c. 1774, Late Victorian formal garden, including parterre c. 1888, H. A. Tipping c. 1930, Dame Syliva Crowe 1972.CSB<br>\n<br>\n2. This garden is depicted on the Second Edition Ordnance Survey 25-inch map of Montgomeryshire XXXVI, sheet  2 (1902). Its main elements on that map include  formal, bridge, carriage drive, croquet lawn, a possible second formal garden, greenhouses, parkland, parterres, reservoir, relict Hegelians, kitchen garden, statue, nursery, terrace walls, walk, a possible second walk, walled garden, woodland, woodland with vista paths and a sunken garden.<br>\nC.S.Briggs 23.05.06<br>\n', 'resourceinstanceid': 'e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Gregynog Hall, Garden, Tregynon', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '265565', 'tiles': [{'tileid': 'cad056d6-ceaa-4f1e-bf36-aeac86314166', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f64-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': '2132df20-ee64-4ee2-a8d7-182576e4590a', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': UUID('cad056d6-ceaa-4f1e-bf36-aeac86314166'), 'data': {'60120f3d-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': 'eaf6969d-f2a3-49d7-9323-77ac5738522c'}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f3d-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': '1faa13dc-c509-4086-aac8-de1e477456d1', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': UUID('cad056d6-ceaa-4f1e-bf36-aeac86314166'), 'data': {'60120f61-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': 'f3dba22b-cb9d-4d0b-89d8-5e21b1f6efd5'}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f61-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': 'a1b67a96-beb3-45b2-8018-dda9111cdafa', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': UUID('cad056d6-ceaa-4f1e-bf36-aeac86314166'), 'data': {'60120f46-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': 'e1824926-a13d-488d-98c9-9fa150db283d'}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f46-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': '543a4129-fd86-4d5a-98e9-39d8501e5b4a', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {'60120f4f-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': 265565.0}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f4f-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': '91ae7b01-4fe7-40c4-916b-dc0879169142', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {'60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': None, '60120f6e-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': 'Parklands & Gardens of Wales No:PGW.PO33    <br>\nPark/gardens/landscape features associated with Gregynog Hall (Nprn29283).<br>\nAssociated with: Earthwork features WNW of Hall (Nprn400946).<br>\nRCAHMW AP94-CS 0071<br>\n<br>\n1. GREGYNOG Is one of the most important gardens and parks Formal and informal woodland garden,  in Powys incorporating various historic overlays dating from at least 1500.  William Emes produced proposals in 1774 and some of them were carried out. In 1920 it became the home of the artistic patrons Gwendoline and Margaret Davies.  H. A. Tipping worked on the gardens 1930-33 and Dame Sylvia Crowe in 1972. Dates and creators are c. 1500 on.  House rebuilt c. 1830 and c. 1880. with landscaping/garden making: William Emes c. 1774, Late Victorian formal garden, including parterre c. 1888, H. A. Tipping c. 1930, Dame Syliva Crowe 1972.CSB<br>\n<br>\n2. This garden is depicted on the Second Edition Ordnance Survey 25-inch map of Montgomeryshire XXXVI, sheet  2 (1902). Its main elements on that map include  formal, bridge, carriage drive, croquet lawn, a possible second formal garden, greenhouses, parkland, parterres, reservoir, relict Hegelians, kitchen garden, statue, nursery, terrace walls, walk, a possible second walk, walled garden, woodland, woodland with vista paths and a sunken garden.<br>\nC.S.Briggs 23.05.06<br>\n', '60120f70-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': '7a82d020-e0f5-4459-b07f-d1e634547fa1'}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': '74b6a2e7-915a-482b-9398-fcbfd1f192de', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f40-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': '999b8b05-89ca-415d-af34-b3f85cf8ffa1', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': UUID('74b6a2e7-915a-482b-9398-fcbfd1f192de'), 'data': {'60120f6a-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': None, '60120f77-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': {'type': 'FeatureCollection', 'features': [{'id': '7cacdc89-9df8-4610-b8b9-f0b250a90980', 'type': 'Feature', 'geometry': {'type': 'Point', 'coordinates': [-3.3513828, 52.566965]}, 'properties': {}}]}}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f6a-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': 'cb9e6cee-0260-4ce3-b476-d2e44dcd0ae9', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {'084fae54-9ff6-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': 'SO0897', '20bd6de6-9ff6-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': 'SO09NE', '688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': None, 'ad6df3ec-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': '9927bd78-9c99-47f1-9feb-9cc361fe0f16'}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('688529e4-9ff5-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': 'f22e0729-7431-4fbc-92fc-5bcee72c173e', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {'60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': '84a97f23-a0f3-4e8e-8dc4-903fa8462db6', '60120f71-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': None, '60120f72-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': '078fdac7-cb0c-4ab6-b252-0db193d97a9c', '60120f78-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': '54496ff2-4693-4138-ba03-277eff940f11'}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f49-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': '095083b9-9220-4bb8-a652-f0aa580359a7', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {'60120f55-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': '248ae010-35a2-4202-be20-41d0495a8c18', '60120f76-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': '54496ff2-4693-4138-ba03-277eff940f11'}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f55-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': '460bb743-63d6-4dcb-a9fa-5a6556fcdbdd', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('e4e1cf66-6760-4c59-9ca1-d38809c43739'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {'60120f52-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': 'PGW(PO)033', '60120f73-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': '81e65c86-3a30-4989-8df2-f7cd4d7d8516', '60120f74-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': 'f6c80c3a-0352-4d89-8a00-ed6bb9fa7d2a'}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f52-9ff2-