2022-06-20 11:15:34,196 arches.app.search.search WARNING  2022-06-20 11:15:34.194478: WARNING: failed to index document: {'displaydescription': 'There are remains of an extensive late eighteenth-century landscape park at Nannau, with indications of an earlier walled deer park and a scenic walk. There are also remains of an extensive system of paths and rides in what was formerly one of the largest and highest areas of designed landscape in Wales.  Within the site are surviving fragments of ancient woodland and a range of interesting and varied built features survive, including two walled kitchen gardens and a small walled ornamental area. There are also lawned grounds with ponds. It was last developed in the first half of the nineteenth century.<br>\n<br>\nThis garden is depicted on the Second Edition Ordnance Survey 25-inch map of Merionethshire XXXIII, sheet  11 (1901). Its main elements on that map include a walk, woodland with vista paths, lodge, orchard, parkland, ponds, quadrangular enclosure, walled garden, lawns, woodland, sundial, quarry, tower, kennels, spring, ford, deer park, reservoir, possible formal garden and greenhouse.<br>\n<br>\nC.S.Briggs, RCAHMW, 22 May 2006.', 'resourceinstanceid': '3045d7d4-c1b6-4821-8519-4ac92b2c1e0b', 'graph_id': '60120f3c-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704', 'map_popup': 'No preference', 'displayname': 'Nannau: Park, Grounds and Gardens', 'root_ontology_class': 'http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing', 'legacyid': '265209', 'tiles': [{'tileid': '3e19081b-6198-42ff-ae06-2e9cf4c2a97e', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('3045d7d4-c1b6-4821-8519-4ac92b2c1e0b'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f64-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': 'd28044e8-967d-488b-9ffd-aa55ac3e5080', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('3045d7d4-c1b6-4821-8519-4ac92b2c1e0b'), 'parenttile_id': UUID('3e19081b-6198-42ff-ae06-2e9cf4c2a97e'), 'data': {'60120f3d-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704':