unds remain partly as public park.  It is an important survival of much of an attractive Victorian park, in a fine natural setting, on the edge of Machynlleth. Part of the house and environs were claimed from one of its main streets in the mid-nineteenth century.  It includes the footings of an ice house and remains of rose and walled gardens. The mansion house became home to the marquesses of Londonderry, who owned extensive estates in the area. House and garden were later given to the town as a public park.  The historical development of the site reflects that of the town , with construction period c. 1841-1900, c. 1948 - pleasure grounds as public park.<br>\n<br>\nThis garden is depicted on the Second Edition Ordnance Survey 25-inch map of Montgomeryshire XXV, sheet  12 (1901). Its main elements on that map include quarry, isolated geometric copses, possible formal garden, lodge, parkland, quadrangular enclosure, kennels and walk.<br>\nC.S.Briggs 23.05.06', '60120f70-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': '7a82d020-e0f5-4459-b07f-d1e634547fa1'}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f43-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': 'bcebc3c6-8171-46e7-86fe-6ef16acb3a4b', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('574a6b42-95aa-44b6-9a6c-08bff68555ed'), 'parenttile_id': None, 'data': {}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f40-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': None}, {'tileid': 'e24586df-14d5-40c9-af2c-8cdf2215f5ab', 'resourceinstance_id': UUID('574a6b42-95aa-44b6-9a6c-08bff68555ed'), 'parenttile_id': UUID('bcebc3c6-8171-46e7-86fe-6ef16acb3a4b'), 'data': {'60120f6a-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': None, '60120f77-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704': {'type': 'FeatureCollection', 'features': [{'id': '963d99b4-e614-4104-925d-e8aec78fded4', 'type': 'Feature', 'geometry': {'type': 'Point', 'coordinates': [-3.8526797, 52.588088]}, 'properties': {}}]}}, 'nodegroup_id': UUID('60120f6a-9ff2-11ea-a530-000d3a86d704'), 'sortorder': 0, 'provisionaledits': N